Subject: [PATCH] mtd: log SPI NOR and SPI NAND IDs at info level
Upstream-Status: Pending

Make manufacturer and device IDs visible in ordinary boot logs for both
SPI flash types. Promote the existing SPI NOR debug message and report
the matched SPI NAND ID after successful detection. For NAND, include
only the manufacturer and device bytes covered by the matched ID length.

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c
@@ -3702,7 +3702,7 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	dev_dbg(dev, "Manufacturer and device ID: %*phN\n",
+	dev_info(dev, "Manufacturer and device ID: %*phN\n",
 		SPI_NOR_MAX_ID_LEN, nor->id);
 
 	return 0;
diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1762,6 +1762,9 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	dev_info(dev, "Manufacturer and device ID: %*phN\n",
+		 spinand->id.len, spinand->id.data);
+
 	if (nand->memorg.ntargets > 1 && !spinand->select_target) {
 		dev_err(dev,
 			"SPI NANDs with more than one die must implement ->select_target()\n");
